  "text": "PetCure Oncology San Antonio, Texas\nPetCure Oncology\nPet Parents: Get Help Now!\nVeterinarians: Refer A Patient\nSearch\nSearch PetCure Oncology\nCancel\nCall us at\n833-738-4376\nPet Cancer\nPet Cancer In Dogs\nPet Cancer In Cats\nPet Cancer Treatment Options\nMaking A Pet Cancer Treatment Decision\nPet Cancer Treatment\nStereotactic Radiation (SRS/SRT) Treatment FAQ\nWhat Makes Us Different?\nWhat To Expect from Treatment\nMedical Oncology\nTelehealth\nClinical Trials & Research\nPayment Resources\nLocations\nPetCure Chicago\nPetCure Clifton, NJ\nPetCure Dallas Fort Worth\nPetCure Phoenix\nPetCure Pittsburgh\nPetCure San Antonio\nPetCure San Jose\nTraveling For Cancer Treatment\nPet Stories\nPet Parent Stories\nShare Your Pet Story\nFor Vets\nRefer a Patient\nComplimentary Imaging Reviews\nAbout Radiation Oncology\nPrimary Care Veterinarians\nB-Cell Lymphoma in Dogs\nNon-Cancerous Conditions\nPost Surgical Radiation\nClinical Information\nCase Studies\nNon-Urgent Questions\nVeterinary FAQ\nAbout\nHistory & Mission\nClinical Leadership\nBusiness Leadership\nContact\nPet Cancer\nPet Cancer In Dogs\nPet Cancer In Cats\nPet Cancer Treatment Options\nMaking A Pet Cancer Treatment Decision\nPet Cancer Treatment\nStereotactic Radiation (SRS/SRT) Treatment FAQ\nWhat Makes Us Different?\nWhat To Expect from Treatment\nMedical Oncology\nTelehealth\nClinical Trials & Research\nPayment Resources\nLocations\nPetCure Chicago\nPetCure Clifton, NJ\nPetCure Dallas Fort Worth\nPetCure Phoenix\nPetCure Pittsburgh\nPetCure San Antonio\nPetCure San Jose\nTraveling For Cancer Treatment\nPet Stories\nPet Parent Stories\nShare Your Pet Story\nFor Vets\nRefer a Patient\nComplimentary Imaging Reviews\nAbout Radiation Oncology\nPrimary Care Veterinarians\nB-Cell Lymphoma in Dogs\nNon-Cancerous Conditions\nPost Surgical Radiation\nClinical Information\nCase Studies\nNon-Urgent Questions\nVeterinary FAQ\nAbout\nHistory & Mission\nClinical Leadership\nBusiness Leadership\nContact\nPet Parents: Get Help Now!\nVeterinarians: Refer A Patient\nSearch PetCure Oncology\n833-738-4376\nPetCure Oncology San Antonio\nPetCure Oncology is proud to announce its newest location, San Antonio, serving pets across south-central Texas and beyond.\nIn addition to the greater San Antonio area, we also welcome those from surrounding states like Louisiana, Arkansas, Oklahoma, and New Mexico. No matter where you’re coming from, you’ll find that our San Antonio facility is a state-of-the-art location, ready to help you and your pet.\nPetCure is located within\nThrive Pet Healthcare Specialists – San Antonio\n, a 30,000-square-foot specialty hospital that also offers 24/7 emergency care and additional specialty services including neurology, internal medicine and advanced diagnostics.\nHow To Make An Appointment\nReach out to us at\n(210) 742-9503\n, or streamline your request by selecting one of the options below:\nPET PARENTS: GET HELP NOW!\nVETERINARIANS: REFER A PATIENT\nYour Care Team\nMedical Director:\nNeal Mauldin, DVM, DACVIM (IM), DACVIM (Oncology), DACVR (RO)\nDr. Neal Mauldin is a triple board-certified veterinary specialist in internal medicine, medical oncology, and radiation oncology.\nBased in Calgary, Alberta, Dr. Mauldin provides remote treatment planning and telemedicine support for PetCure Oncology facilities across the country. He previously spent eight years at Louisiana State University as an associate professor and section head of therapeutic radiology. His advanced training includes veterinary school at Texas A&M University, internships and residencies at the Animal Medical Center in New York City, and a prestigious fellowship in radiation oncology at Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center.\nA lifelong animal lover, Dr. Mauldin is a proud pet parent to Allie, a mixed breed rescued during Hurricane Allison; Shetland Sheepdogs Cami, Jenna, Charlotte, and Tuscan; and his horses Webster, Heston, and Betty Boop.\nLearn more about PetCure Oncology’s clinical specialists\n.\nRadiation Oncologist:\nKelsey Pohlmann, DVM, MS, DACVR (RO)\nDr. Pohlmann is one of PetCure Oncology’s remote radiation oncologists. She oversees teleconsultations and treatment planning for patients and veterinarians in and around New Jersey, as well as nationally for pet owners that do not reside in a region with a PetCure treatment center. Dr. Pohlmann earned her veterinary degree from the University of Georgia before completing her residency in radiation oncology at Colorado State University’s prestigious Flint Animal Cancer Center. She has been working with PetCure Oncology since 2016.\nSupervising Veterinarian:\nTracy Gati, DVM, DABVP (canine and feline), Emergency Founding Fellow ABVP\nDr. Tracy Gati is the Supervising Veterinarian for PetCure San Antonio and is excited to be provided a much-needed service to the pets of south Texas. Dr. Gati has previously been employed as a staff emergency clinician at Thrive Pet Healthcare Specialists and the program director for the San Antonio location of ER Academy, which is an intensive mentorship program for veterinarians entering emergency medicine. She has been a valued member of the team since 2010. Dr. Gati attended the University of Mississippi and Louisiana State University for her undergraduate studies and received her Doctorate of Veterinary Medicine from Louisiana State University in 2003. Dr. Gati is board certified in canine and feline medicine through AVBP and is proud to be a founding fellow in ER specialty through the American Board of Veterinary Practitioners.\nThough she’s proud to hail from Louisiana she considers herself a converted Texan and loves calling San Antonio home.  Dr. Gati enjoys spending time with her husband, 2 children, 2 dogs and 3 cats.  She has been a Girl Scout troop leader since 2015 and her favorite thing to do is go camping with her girls.  In her spare time, she can be found shuttling her kids around the city, reading and hiking.\nPractice Manager:\nGemma Clarkson\nSchedule Coordinator:\nBlair S.\nRadiation Therapist:\nChristina G, R.T.(T)\nVeterinary Technician:\nMonica S, LVT\nVeterinary Technician:\nSarah H.\nTeam Email:\nPetCure.SanAntonio@ThrivePet.com\nProudly Serving the San Antonio, TX Area & Beyond\nWe’re excited to extend a warm welcome to patients from across south and central Texas and surrounding areas to our San Antonio location. Our doors are open to everyone, whether you’re a local from the San Antonio area or from farther away in neighboring towns or even neighboring states. Pet patients and their families visit us from all over, including, but not limited to, these fantastic communities:\nAlamo Heights\nAustin\nBoerne\nBrownsville\nCorpus Christi\nDel Rio\nEagle Pass\nFredericksburg\nHarlingen\nKerrville\nLaredo\nMcAllen\nNew Braunfels\nSan Marcos\nSeguin\nVictoria\nand surrounding areas\nIf You Are Traveling From Out-Of-Town\nWe want to make your visit as easy and stress-free as possible. If you would like assistance finding\npet-friendly hotels and restaurants nearby\n, we are happy to help. Also, see our\nTips for Traveling With Your Pet for Cancer Treatment\n. If you have any other questions, simply ask one of our client service representatives or visit our\ncomprehensive guide to traveling to San Antonio\nwith your pet.\nPRESS RELEASE:\nPetCure Oncology San Antonio\n2426 Ceegee St\nSan Antonio, TX, 78217\nPhone: (210) 742-9503\nFax:\nEmail:\nPetCure.SanAntonio@ThrivePet.com\nWebsite:\npetcureoncology.com/locations/san-antonio/\nGet Directions\nMore Locations\nVeterinary Cancer Group\nPetCure Oncology San Antonio\nPetCure Oncology Clifton NJ\nPetCure Oncology Chicago\nPetCure Oncology Phoenix\nPetCure Oncology Pittsburgh\nPetCure Oncology San Jose\nPetCure Oncology Dallas Fort Worth\nMore Than 10,000 Pet Families Have Chosen PetCure Oncology For Their Dog Or Cat's Cancer Therapy. We Give Your Pet A Fighting Chance To Improve Their Quality Of Life.\nWe Understand. We Commit. We Will Help.\nPET PARENTS: GET HELP NOW!\nVETERINARIANS REFER A PATIENT\n833-738-4376\nSRS/SRT FAQ\nVets FAQ\nContact\nNews\nPress Room\nCareers\nFacebook\nInstagram\nTikTok\nLinkedIn\nSIGN UP FOR NEWSLETTER\nAt PetCure Oncology we are unconditionally committed to delivering industry-leading cancer care to pets and unwavering support to the families who love them. Pet families are given guidance, knowledge, and access to comprehensive and compassionate pet cancer care. Together with our pet patients and their families, we share in the cancer journey. We believe pet parents deserve the best clinical expertise and advanced treatment options for their pets.\nPrivacy Notice\n|\nTerms of Use\n|\nDisclaimer Notice\n|\nYour Privacy Choices\nCopyright ©2026\nPetCure Oncology\n. All Rights Reserved.\nNEED ANSWERS? WE'RE HERE FOR YOU.\nCall\n833-738-4376\nnow to speak with a member of the Pet Advocate Team.\nBACK TO TOP",
